            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_236N2015A">
               <eventList type="performances" xml:id="eventList_5f14503d">
                  <event xml:id="event_fb30d8e7">
                     <date isodate="1880-02-21" xml:id="date_N2047C">1880-02-21</date>
                     <geogName role="venue" xml:id="geogName_177afafe">St. Johannes Kirke</geogName>
                     <geogName role="place" xml:id="geogName_56092b44">Copenhagen</geogName>
                     <persName role="" xml:id="persName_528c2aab">Hr. Levinsen, song</persName>
                     <persName role="" xml:id="persName_04b64a7e">Gottfred Matthison-Hansen, organ</persName>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_f4f4e1a8">
                        <head xml:id="head_N20496">Reviews</head>
                     </biblList>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_dc657dce">
                        <head xml:id="head_N204B2">Evidence</head>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm202">In 1837 Hartmann participated in Musikforeningen's  competition on "den bedste Samling af 6 Sange over forskjellige nærmere bestemte Texter." His contributions were: No. 1 "Indvielsen"; No. 2 "Hvad toner gjennem Skoven"; No. 3 "Langsad Strandveien"; No. 4 "Til de Døde"; No. 5 "Lille Cathrine" and No. 6 "Flyv, Fugl, flyv". Nos. 1 and 4-6 were chosen for publication by the jury, whereas Nos. 2 &amp; 3 remained unpublished.</p>
            </history>
